==Russian==

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*dorgъ}}. {{doublet|ru|драго́й}}, a borrowing from Old Church Slavonic.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|дорого́й}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-дорогой.ogg}}

====Adjective====
{{ru-adj|дорого́й|доро́же|дорожа́йший|adv=до́рого|adv2=втри́дорога|adv3=за́дорого|adv4=задо́рого|adv5=лю́бо-до́рого|absn=дорогови́зна|aug=дорогу́щий|attenu=дорогова́тый}}

# [[dear]], [[precious]]
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1930|author=w:ru:Нина Берберова<t:{{w|Nina Berberova}}>|title=Последние и первые|chapter=IV|location=Paris|publisher=Jacques Povolozky & Cie|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Marian Schwartz|title2=The Last and the First|location2=London|publisher2=w:Pushkin Press|year2=2021|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=И она́ посмотре́ла на него́ так, сло́вно хоте́ла в па́мяти его́ воскреси́ть '''дороги́е''' и гро́зные мгнове́ния.|t=And she looked at him as if she wanted to resurrect '''precious''' and terrible moments in her memory.}}
# [[expensive]]
#: {{ant|ru|дешёвый}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1869|author=w:ru:Иван Гончаров<t:{{w|Ivan Goncharov}}>|title=w:ru:[[Обрыв (роман)|Обрыв]]|chapter=[[s:ru:Обрыв_(Гончаров)/Часть_I/Глава_XIII|Часть I. Глава XIII]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=Stephen Pearl|title2=w:en:[[The Precipice (Goncharov novel)|Malinovka Heights]]|location2=|publisher2=Alma Classics|year2=2020|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=Е́сли случа́йно попадёт туда́ высокой ки́сти карти́на, '''дорога́я''' ста́туя — они́ це́нятся не удивле́нием ки́сти и резцу́, а запла́ченной су́ммой.|t=If by chance the apartment happened to contain a painting by a reputable artist, or an '''expensive''' piece of statuary, it would be valued not by an appreciation of its merits as a work of art, but for how much it cost.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In the sense of "my [[dear]]", this word is not restricted to use between men and women, but is quite common between friends of the same sex, or a teacher to any of his students without regard to sex. When used between men, {{m|ru||[[мой]] [[дорогой]]}} usually is not translated, since English does not possess a good unisex counterpart to this.

